 "notes": "Two real problems surfaced only by a run against a real database, not by this local sandbox's default (no DATABASE_URL) jest run: (1) TasksService.delete() hit Prisma P2003 (task_execution_state FK, onDelete: Restrict) for any task that ever entered in_progress \u2014 fixed by converting it to a 409 ConflictException rather than routing around the DB's intentional protection of the execution audit trail. (2) task_execution_transitions and task_outbox_events turned out to be DB-trigger-enforced append-only (BEFORE UPDATE OR DELETE RAISE EXCEPTION), not just FK-restrict \u2014 transitively making task_execution_attempts/state, and therefore the task itself, permanently undeletable once any transition is recorded. That is a genuine, deliberate, previously-unexercised consequence of this card's wiring, not a bug: a task that ever enters in_progress after this ships can never be deleted via the API again (returns 409). tasks-agent-scope.e2e.spec.ts's own cleanup hit both issues in turn; fixed by excluding tasks with a recorded transition from its own task.deleteMany rather than trying to delete rows the database will never allow deleted. Verified this specific claim against a real local Postgres (targeted_test-tasks_agent_scope), not asserted from reading the trigger SQL alone: reproduced the exact CI failure locally, applied the fix, confirmed 26/26 passing. Separately, the mutation-evidence.spec.ts git-snapshot fingerprint (apps/api/test/assembly/mutation-results.json's supplementalGit) was computed locally before `git add`-ing 5 new files on the first attempt, so `git add -u` (update-only) silently excluded them from the hash \u2014 refreshed correctly (self-referential stability confirmed each time) on every commit since; not itself part of this receipt's impact set (test-fixture-owned evidence, uncovered_files per impact0) but recorded here since it was the other cause of local-vs-CI drift on this branch. UPDATE 2026-09-09T15:47Z: the 15 not_measured entities from the prior version of this receipt are now resolved per DEC-AUP-0010 (no operator gates) \u2014 13 apps/web nodes via a real read-only canary probe against production (see canary-tasks-route-production), 2 deployable_unit nodes via a typed, owned, expiring exemption (PRE_MERGE_DEPLOY_GATE_NOT_APPLICABLE) since can-i-deploy is a deploy-time question this repo's own `deploy` CI job already owns. admission.verdict is now admitted_with_exemptions.",
